 ## Overview
-Allocates GPU memory and loads the opacity transfer function (TF) table, or reloads it if the transfer function has changed [S1, unofficial]. It ensures the transfer function data is monotonic in opacity to support DDA (Digital Differential Analyzer) optimizations, then uploads the data to the GPU via an SSBO and configures the necessary shader uniforms [S2, unofficial]. It differs from [Transfer Function Loading](4289-transfer-function-loading.md) by focusing on the GPU upload, monotonicity enforcement, and uniform binding rather than file I/O and parsing.
+Allocates GPU memory and loads the opacity transfer function (TF) table, or reloads it if the transfer function has changed [S1, unofficial]. It uploads the transfer function LUT to the GPU and checks if the alpha values are monotonically non-decreasing; if not, it applies a Cumulative Distribution Function (CDF) transformation before uploading [S2, unofficial]. This transformation is required for Digital Differential Analyzer (DDA) optimizations [S2, unofficial]. It differs from [Transfer Function Loading](4289-transfer-function-loading.md) by focusing on the memory management, monotonicity enforcement, and state binding rather than file I/O and parsing.
 
